course: dictionary
lesson: 15600
title: Takings: the money a shop makes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Takings are the money a shop, cafe, fair or business gets from selling things in a certain time. «The cake stall's takings were £32 at the school fair.» Here takings means the money the stall took in from selling cakes.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. The day's takings, a school fair, a cake stall: these are all places where people buy things. So takings must be about money coming in from sales.
explain: To work out takings, add up the money from each sale, or multiply the price by the number sold. If 5 cakes cost 40p each, the takings are 5 × 40p, which is £2. Always ask: is this the money coming in?
fact: Takings means the money taken in from selling things in a set time.
fact: Takings is a plural noun, so we say «the takings were», not «the takings was».
fact: To find takings, add each sale together, or multiply price × number sold.
fact: «Takings» is common in the UK and Australia; in the US people more often say «receipts» or «sales».
exercise: «Mrs Patel counted the day's takings at the end of the shop.» What are takings? | *The money a shop gets from selling things | The tax the shop pays to the government | The goods left on the shelves | The number of customers who came in
exercise: A cake stall sells 6 cakes at 50p each. What are the takings? | £0.56 | £6.00 | *£3.00 | £30.00
exercise: In the US, people more often say what instead of takings? | shelves | cakes | change | *sales
test: «The school fair's takings went to the library fund.» What does takings mean here? | The prizes given away at the fair | The gifts people brought | The games children played | *The money taken in from selling things
test: Maya sells 10 raffle tickets at £1 each. What are her takings? | £11 | £1 | *£10 | £100
exam: «The café's takings were £85 on Saturday.» Which is true? | *The café made £85 from selling things | The café lost £85 on the day | The café gave £85 away in free food | The café spent £85 on cups and plates
